OpenWings patch 0019: the app shows the OpenWings name and logo

The project is named OpenWings: two open black wings on a white tile
(docs/brand/). The web app showed upstream's name, Odysseus, and its boat
logo. This patch changes what a person sees; it keeps every technical
name (WINGS_* settings, the wings package, the Docker project and its
volumes), so existing installs keep their data and settings.

  * static/index.html: page and tab titles, the sidebar name, the welcome
    screen logo and name, the message box placeholder, the favicon (black
    wings on a white tile whatever the accent color) and two settings
    labels say OpenWings.
  * static/login.html: the OpenWings logo and name, and a "built on
    Odysseus (AGPL 3.0)" line linking to upstream.
  * static/manifest.json: the installed app is named OpenWings. The image
    build replaces upstream's app icons and favicon with OpenWings ones
    (docker/odysseus/Dockerfile copies them from wings/brand).
  * static/js/theme.js: the theme no longer repaints the favicon as the
    boat in the accent color; the main pages keep the wings tile (route
    icons such as calendar and notes are unchanged).
  * static/app.js: the message box placeholder says OpenWings.
  * static/js/chat.js, chatRenderer.js, slashCommands.js: the assistant's
    label on system replies says OpenWings.
  * src/tool_schemas.py, src/tool_index.py, src/secret_storage.py,
    scripts/generate_env_reference.py: tool descriptions and messages
    name the OpenWings browser and code runner.

Unchanged on purpose: the "Odysseus" character preset (a persona, the king
of Ithaca) and the "You are Odysseus." line in upstream's model prompts,
which upstream's own tuned models may expect.

Applies to: odysseus-dev/odysseus@9d0d3720f4ca181d87bef94da826d730acc6d483
License: AGPL-3.0-or-later (same as upstream)

